prctl: report the program's no_new_privs flag, not PRoot's

PRoot sets no_new_privs itself to install its seccomp filter, so
prctl(PR_GET_NO_NEW_PRIVS) reported 1 to every program. Answer it with
the flag the program inherited from PRoot's caller or set itself.

Offered upstream as proot-me/proot#448; drop this file once it lands.
It is made against proot-execfn-auxv.patch, which touches the same code.
